                <pb facs="0410" n="306" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4163b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-12T16:00:00-05:00">February 12, 1932—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. For the Minister and Consul-General. For your confidential information and
                    guidance.</p>
                <p>Reference Department’s telegram to the American Consul, Shanghai, No. 13 of
                    February 10, 8 p.m.</p>
                <p>The Department has today telegraphed Minister Wilson at Geneva, for discreet communication to Drummond, in part as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Any effort which any agency may make at this time toward the objective
                            of bringing the hostilities to an end will have my approval in
                            principle”.</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
